deep.reconstruction:
The page continues the computation from p.29. There, for X over S, the sheaf $\widetilde{X^{
u+1}}$ on the 'DR-stratifying' site is ind-represented. Its pieces are the PD-neighbourhoods $\Delta^{(
u)}_{X/S}(i)(j)$: the j-th divided-power level of the PD-envelope of the i-th infinitesimal neighbourhood of the diagonal in $X^{
u+1}$. Page 29 ends with the claim, marked 'à vérifier', that $H^q(\widetilde{(U,U')},\mathcal O)=H^q(U',\mathcal O_{U'})$ for each object (U,U') of the site; this page opens by finishing that sentence.

Step 1. If X (over S) is affine, all the pieces are affine. Hence $H^q(\widetilde{X^{
u+1}},\mathcal O)=0$ for q>0. Also $H^0(\widetilde{X^{
u+1}},\mathcal O)=\varprojlim_{i,j}H^0(\Delta^{(
u)}_{X/S}(i)(j),\mathcal O)$, i.e. sections over an ind-object are the projective limit of the sections over its pieces.

Step 2. The $\widetilde{X^{
u+1}}$ form the Čech nerve of the covering $\widetilde X	o e$ of the final object. Čech-to-derived comparison then gives $H^n(X_{DR\,strat},\mathcal O)\simeq H^n(
u\mapsto H^0(\widetilde{X^{
u+1}}_{/X}))$. This is the cohomology of the cosimplicial ring of completed PD-envelopes of the diagonals: the Čech–Alexander complex.

Step 3. For general (non-affine) X, the same construction sheafifies Zariski-locally. One gets a cosimplicial sheaf of rings on X, augmented over $\mathcal O_X$ and carrying divided powers, denoted $\mathcal E^*$. Then $H^*(X_{DR\,strat},\mathcal O)\simeq\mathbb H^*(X_{Zar},\mathcal E^*)$.

Purpose: compute crystalline (PD-stratified de Rham) cohomology of $\mathcal O$ explicitly as the Zariski hypercohomology of a 'formal/PD completion of the diagonal' cosimplicial algebra. This is the PD analogue of Grothendieck's description of infinitesimal/de Rham cohomology via the formal completion of $X^{
u+1}$ along the diagonal. The next page begins the universal construction of PD-envelopes needed to make $\Delta(i)(j)$ precise.

